cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Replication package for "Short episodes, asymmetric payoffs: forecasting negative electricity
  prices and the market premium in Germany"
message: If you use this software or data, please cite the archived release.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
authors:
  - given-names: Suho
    family-names: Ahn
    email: dkstngh3502@kaist.ac.kr
    affiliation: School of Business and Technology Management, KAIST
    country: KR
repository-code: https://github.com/suhoahn-web/negative-price-forecasting-de
license: MIT
keywords:
  - negative electricity prices
  - electricity price forecasting
  - market premium
  - cost-loss ratio
  - forecast value
  - rare-event classification
abstract: >-
  Code and the archived data vintage reproducing all tables and figures of a study of
  negative-price episodes in the German day-ahead electricity market. The study measures the
  duration distribution of those episodes, forecasts the event that suspends the renewable
  market premium under section 51 of the German Renewable Energy Sources Act, and evaluates
  the economic value of such a forecast using a cost-loss framework. Classifiers are estimated
  on a rolling 730-day window and refitted monthly, which is the scheme required by the
  Giacomini-White test of conditional predictive ability used for inference. Data are public,
  from the Energy-Charts API operated by Fraunhofer ISE under CC BY 4.0.
